{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1911","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1911","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1911\",\"parent_revision\":\"7121ceb7f3505504ee145ab34e0af44b5c5808a1\",\"root_revision\":\"e2a5f088d0d77f3f55b23e296a5bcb7579228e994cb8e06abf9d0127967c4e5f\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nClaim 1: No single-invocation skill quality improvement workflow exists in plugin-creator\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n- claim: No skill or agent exists that chains skilllint, audit-skill-completeness, audit-skill-lifecycle, and improvement routing in one invocation\\n- evidence: backlog_list search for \\\"skill quality improve unified workflow\\\" returned only #1911; Read tool confirmed plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ directory has no improve-skill, quality-improve, or skill-qa directory; plugin-lifecycle/SKILL.md routing table has no improve entry at line 22 routing table section\\n- source: plugins/plugin-creator/CLAUDE.md (read lines 1-60), plugins/plugin-creator/skills/plugin-lifecycle/SKILL.md (lines 1-50)\\n\\nClaim 2: All constituent tools (audit-skill-completeness, audit-skill-lifecycle, write-frontmatter-description, refactor-skill, ensure-complete, assessor) exist as standalone skills\\n- verdict: VERIFIED\\n- claim: Each constituent tool exists as a callable skill or agent in the plugin-creator plugin\\n- evidence: Read tool confirmed presence of SKILL.md files at: plugins/plugin-creator/skills/audit-skill-completeness/SKILL.md (user-invocable: true, line 6), plugins/plugin-creator/skills/plugin-lifecycle/SKILL.md (user-invocable: true)\\n- source: plugins/plugin-creator/skills/audit-skill-completeness/SKILL.md (lines 1-8), plugins/plugin-creator/skills/plugin-lifecycle/SKILL.md (lines 1-8)\\n\\nClaim 3: contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer agent exists and is relevant\\n- verdict: VERIFIED (from #1899 fact-check, 2026-04-26)\\n- claim: contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer bundles optimization, audit, and frontmatter writing concerns\\n- evidence: #1899 fact-check results (Claim 1) confirmed agent file at plugins/plugin-creator/agents/contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer.md, description names only one concern, skills array proves three bundled concerns\\n- source: plugins/plugin-creator/agents/contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer.md (lines 2-8, per #1899 fact-check)\\n\\nClaim 4: The item depends on the agent split in #1899 (skill-auditor, ai-doc-optimizer, skill-content-updater)\\n- verdict: INCONCLUSIVE\\n- claim: Item description states this depends on the agent split in #1899\\n- evidence: #1899 is groomed; constituent agents (skill-auditor, skill-content-updater, ai-doc-optimizer) do NOT yet exist on disk \u2014 they are planned work in #1899; however this item's Acceptance Criteria do not cite these new agents and reference only existing tools; the dependency may be aspirational (adopt new agents when available) rather than a hard block\\n- source: backlog_view(#1899) sections_index confirms agents not yet created; this item's Acceptance Criteria section references only existing tools\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: plugin-creator: no single-invocation skill quality improvement workflow\\nDate: 2026-05-02\\nGoal: Confirm information is complete to create a unified orchestrating skill that runs quality improvement passes on a plugin-creator skill or agent in a single invocation\\nConditions:\\n1. Functional intent \u2014 no unified quality improvement invocation exists | Snapshot: AVAILABLE -> Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Existing groomed section (2026-04-26) + backlog_list search confirmed no /plugin-creator:improve-skill or equivalent skill present in plugins/plugin-creator/skills/\\n2. All constituent tools exist and are functional | Snapshot: AVAILABLE -> Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read tool confirmed: audit-skill-completeness/SKILL.md (user-invocable: true), audit-skill-lifecycle/SKILL.md (exists), write-frontmatter-description/SKILL.md (user-invocable: true), refactor-skill/SKILL.md (exists), ensure-complete/SKILL.md (exists), assessor/SKILL.md (exists)\\n3. Invocation surface decision (new skill vs plugin-lifecycle extension vs agent) | Snapshot: MISSING -> Final: MISSING | Citation: Questions for Human section from 2026-04-26 grooming \u2014 this is a human decision gate; no resolution found in backlog history or user messages\\n4. Confirmed ordered sequence of tool invocations | Snapshot: MISSING -> Final: DERIVABLE | Citation: Implementation Notes section from 2026-04-26 grooming documents a candidate 5-step sequence (skilllint -> audit-completeness -> audit-lifecycle -> route -> re-validate); this sequence is derivable from existing skill documentation even if not yet validated end-to-end\\n5. Plugin-lifecycle skill cross-reference exists and covers improve scenario | Snapshot: DERIVABLE -> Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read tool \u2014 plugin-lifecycle/SKILL.md line 14 shows routing table; no improve-skill entry present; this is the gap this item fills\\n6. plugin-creator CLAUDE.md routing table structure | Snapshot: AVAILABLE -> Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read tool \u2014 plugins/plugin-creator/CLAUDE.md routing table confirmed present; can be updated to add improve-skill trigger phrase\\n7. Related item #1899 (skill-update workflow) status | Snapshot: DERIVABLE -> Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: backlog_view(#1899) \u2014 status: groomed; no blocking conditions; independent of this item\\n8. Dependency on #1899 agent split (skill-auditor, ai-doc-optimizer, skill-content-updater) | Snapshot: MISSING -> Final: DERIVABLE | Citation: Item description states \\\"Depends on the agent split in #1899\\\"; however Acceptance Criteria in this item and #1899 confirm constituent tools already exist; the unified workflow can be built on current tools and adopt new agents when #1899 ships\\nChanges from snapshot (2026-04-26):\\n- Condition 4: MISSING -> DERIVABLE (Implementation Notes section provides a candidate sequence)\\n- Condition 7: DERIVABLE -> AVAILABLE (backlog_view confirmed #1899 groomed status)\\n- Condition 8: MISSING -> DERIVABLE (item can proceed with existing tools; #1899 adoption is additive)\\nAVAILABLE count: 5\\nDERIVABLE count: 2\\nMISSING count: 1\\nDecision: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS \u2014 one MISSING condition (invocation surface decision) requires human input before implementation can begin; planning can proceed; implementation gate (rt-ica) will halt until human resolves this\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **plugin-creator: no single-invocation skill quality improvement workflow; bringing a skill or agent toward best practice requires manually running multiple unconnected tools** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 2026-04-23; fixing finalize.md required running optimizer after writing instead of before; agent content extraction and language auditing have no combined invocation path\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-23\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-26)\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n8/10 \u2014 P1. Every skill quality improvement session requires manually chaining 4-6 separate tools in the correct order. The plugin-creator plugin creates skills but provides no unified path to improve them. The problem is observable and recurring: finalize.md was written without loading skill writing guidelines, producing advisory prose and a correctness bug; the optimizer was run afterward as remediation. The correct automated path did not exist.\\n\\n**Effort**: Medium \u2014 all constituent tools exist and work independently; the implementation is orchestration wiring plus a new SKILL.md or an extension to plugin-lifecycle. Scope is Small-Medium if extending plugin-lifecycle; Medium if creating a new skill with a full decision-routing workflow. One MISSING condition (invocation surface decision) must be resolved by human before implementation design can proceed.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nWhen invoked with a path to a skill directory or agent file, the unified workflow:\\n\\n1. Validates structure and frontmatter via skilllint \u2014 reports and resolves structural errors\\n2. Audits completeness against best-practice categories via audit-skill-completeness \u2014 establishes baseline score\\n3. Audits semantic lifecycle coherence via audit-skill-lifecycle \u2014 identifies call chain gaps, circular refs, duplications\\n4. Routes to the appropriate improvement action based on findings: description rewrite, references extraction, skill split, or content optimization\\n5. Executes the selected improvement action\\n6. Re-validates to confirm the score improved\\n\\nAll steps happen in one invocation. The user observes a before score, the improvements applied, and an after score \u2014 without needing to know which tools were invoked internally.\\n\\n### Desired Structure\\n\\nAn observable target state (verifiable without reading code):\\n\\n- A single slash command (e.g., /plugin-creator:improve-skill path) exists and appears in tab-autocomplete\\n- Running it on a skill with known quality gaps produces a scored report and applies improvements in one session\\n- The command is listed in the plugin CLAUDE.md routing table under a clear trigger phrase\\n- Before and after scores from uvx skilllint@latest check and audit-skill-completeness are reported in the session\\n- The workflow terminates without requiring the user to know which constituent tools exist\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. Running the unified improvement command on a skill with a known quality gap produces a scored report and applies at least one improvement without additional user commands\\n2. After the workflow completes, uvx skilllint@latest check exits 0 on the target skill (no new errors introduced; pre-existing warnings acceptable)\\n3. After the workflow completes, /plugin-creator:audit-skill-completeness shows a completeness score equal to or higher than the pre-run score\\n4. The workflow reports what it changed (diff or summary) before applying changes \u2014 no silent overwrites\\n5. The workflow is discoverable: grep -n \\\"improve-skill\\\\|quality-improve\\\\|skill-qa\\\" plugins/plugin-creator/CLAUDE.md returns at least one line\\n6. The workflow can be invoked by a user or agent that does not know which underlying tools exist \u2014 constituent tools are orchestrated internally, not exposed as a manual sequence\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:lint |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:audit-skill-completeness |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:audit-skill-lifecycle |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:write-frontmatter-description |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:refactor-skill |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:ensure-complete |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:plugin-lifecycle |\\n| Skill | /plugin-creator:assessor |\\n| Agent | @plugin-creator:contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer |\\n| Prior work | plugins/plugin-creator/CLAUDE.md |\\n| Prior work | plugins/plugin-creator/skills/plugin-lifecycle/SKILL.md |\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: Invocation surface decision (new skill vs plugin-lifecycle extension vs agent) \u2014 human decision required before implementation design can proceed; this is the sole MISSING RT-ICA condition\\n- Depends on: #1899 (plugin-creator: no single-invocation skill update workflow) \u2014 ASPIRATIONAL dependency only; current implementation can use existing constituent tools; when #1899 ships its skill-auditor and skill-content-updater agents, the unified workflow can adopt them as upgraded orchestration targets without restructuring\\n- Blocks: None identified in open backlog\\n- Related: #1908 (reference drift checking) \u2014 mentioned in item description as a quality dimension that belongs in a combined quality pass; #1908 is tracked separately\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nMedium \u2014 all constituent tools exist and work independently; the implementation is orchestration wiring plus a new SKILL.md or an extension to plugin-lifecycle. Scope is Small-Medium if extending plugin-lifecycle; Medium if creating a new skill with a full decision-routing workflow.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 AI-facing routing table; must include improve-skill trigger phrase to make the unified workflow discoverable by orchestrators\\n\\n### Blockers\\n\\n- MISSING: Invocation surface decision (new skill vs plugin-lifecycle extension vs agent) \u2014 requires human input before implementation design can proceed\\n- MISSING: Confirmed ordered sequence of tool invocations \u2014 requires a discovery task mapping the current manual workflow\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- None \u2014 the unified workflow orchestrates existing tools; it does not change their interfaces\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/CLAUDE.md` \u2014 routing table updated to add trigger phrase for improve-skill entry point regardless of which surface option is chosen\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/` \u2014 new skill directory (e.g., improve-skill/) with SKILL.md to be created (if invocation surface decision is Option A: new skill)\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/plugin-lifecycle/SKILL.md` \u2014 extended with improvement workflow section (if invocation surface decision is Option B: extend plugin-lifecycle)\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\n- `.claude-plugin/plugin.json` and `marketplace.json` \u2014 auto-bumped by pre-commit hook when new skill directory is added (Option A only); no change for Option B\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\n**Alignment assessment**: NOT_APPLICABLE\\n\\nThis is a new feature item \u2014 no existing implementation exists to compare against the design intent. The target artifact (unified quality improvement skill or plugin-lifecycle extension) does not yet exist in the codebase.\\n\\nObservable confirmation:\\n- grep -rn \\\"improve-skill\\\\|skill-qa\\\\|quality-improve\\\" plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ returns no output (no such skill exists yet)\\n- plugin-lifecycle/SKILL.md routing table does not include an improvement workflow entry\\n\\nNo divergence from design intent is possible when the implementation has not started. Design intent is well-specified in Desired Structure and Acceptance Criteria sections (from 2026-04-26 grooming). The invocation surface decision (new skill vs extension) is the one remaining open question that shapes the implementation path.\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\n- `plugins/plugin-creator/skills/plugin-lifecycle/SKILL.md` \u2014 if Option B: extended; if Option A: gains a cross-reference pointer to the new improve-skill entry point\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated to new interface\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every agent instruction updated\\n- [ ] Old interface deprecated or removed (if replacing)\\n- [ ] CI/config files updated and validated\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n### Implementation Notes\\n\\nOrchestration flow (constituent tools to unify):\\n\\n1. Measure (uvx skilllint@latest check path) \u2014 structural gate; report token count and error codes\\n2. Audit completeness (/plugin-creator:audit-skill-completeness path) \u2014 establish baseline score\\n3. Audit lifecycle (/plugin-creator:audit-skill-lifecycle plugin-path) \u2014 semantic gap detection\\n4. Route to improvement action based on findings:\\n   - SK007 error \u2192 /plugin-creator:refactor-skill (split required)\\n   - SK006 warning + cohesive content \u2192 references/ extraction in refactor-skill\\n   - Description quality gap \u2192 /plugin-creator:write-frontmatter-description\\n   - Content/clarity gap \u2192 @plugin-creator:contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer\\n5. Re-validate (uvx skilllint@latest check + audit-skill-completeness) \u2014 confirm improvement\\n\\nMISSING: Invocation surface decision (human input required before implementation proceeds).\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: missing-guardrail\\n**Rationale**: The system has all the constituent tools needed to bring a skill to best practice (skilllint, audit-skill-completeness, audit-skill-lifecycle, write-frontmatter-description, refactor-skill) but no combined invocation path. Skills and agents accumulate quality debt because the correct improvement path has no automated entry point \u2014 a developer must know which tools exist, their correct invocation order, and how to interpret their combined output. This is a guardrail (consolidated workflow) that was never created. No traceable failure event; the same class of problem (missing unified quality workflow) is not found in prior resolved issues for plugin-creator.\\n**Analysis Method**: No RCA required for missing-guardrail type\\n**Scenario Target**: Skill author wants to improve a skill's quality -> currently must manually chain 4-6 separate tool invocations in undocumented order -> improvement: single /improve-skill invocation that orchestrates all passes internally and reports before/after score\\n\\n### Questions for Human\\n\\n- Should the unified improvement workflow be: (A) a new slash command like /plugin-creator:improve-skill, (B) an extension to /plugin-creator:plugin-lifecycle, or (C) a new agent? This decision gates all implementation design.\\n- Is there a preferred name for the new entry point? (e.g., improve-skill, quality-improve, skill-qa)\\n- Should the workflow be fully autonomous (apply all improvements automatically) or interactive (show findings and ask before applying each)?\\n- Are there quality dimensions beyond skilllint + audit-skill-completeness + audit-skill-lifecycle that the unified workflow should cover?\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n**Status: APPROVED-WITH-GAPS**\\n\\n| Dimension | Status | Evidence |\\n|-----------|--------|----------|\\n| Functional intent | AVAILABLE | Item title and description clearly state the problem: no unified workflow for skill quality improvement |\\n| Scope boundaries | PARTIAL | plugin-creator plugin named; invocation surface (new skill vs plugin-lifecycle extension vs agent) not specified |\\n| External interfaces | AVAILABLE | All constituent tools confirmed in codebase: uvx skilllint@latest, /plugin-creator:audit-skill-completeness, /plugin-creator:audit-skill-lifecycle, /plugin-creator:write-frontmatter-description, /plugin-creator:refactor-skill, /plugin-creator:ensure-complete, @plugin-creator:contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer |\\n| Constraints | DERIVABLE | plugin-creator patterns (skills as orchestrators), skill size limits (SK006/SK007), progressive disclosure design \u2014 derivable from existing plugin |\\n| Existing system context | AVAILABLE | plugin-creator CLAUDE.md and all skill SKILL.md files read; routing table, component inventory confirmed |\\n\\nMissing inputs:\\n1. Invocation surface \u2014 new skill, plugin-lifecycle extension, or agent (human decision required)\\n2. Confirmed ordered tool sequence (discovery task needed)\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\nN/A for feature items \u2014 no defect to reproduce.\\n\\nObservable gap verification (confirms the workflow is absent):\\n1. Run: ls plugins/plugin-creator/skills/ | grep -E \\\"improve|quality-improve|skill-qa\\\"\\n   Expected: no output (no such skill directory exists)\\n2. Run: grep -n \\\"improve-skill\\\\|quality-improve\\\\|skill-qa\\\" plugins/plugin-creator/CLAUDE.md\\n   Expected: no output (no trigger phrase in routing table)\\nBoth commands returning empty output confirm the gap described in the item is present.\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a skill or agent author (human or AI orchestrator), I want a single invocation that assesses a plugin-creator skill or agent against all best-practice dimensions and applies the appropriate improvement action, so I do not have to manually chain skilllint, audit-skill-completeness, audit-skill-lifecycle, write-frontmatter-description, and refactor-skill in the correct order each time.\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- audit-skill-completeness/SKILL.md: constituent tool; not modified; orchestrated via existing skill invocation\\n- audit-skill-lifecycle/SKILL.md: constituent tool; not modified; orchestrated\\n- write-frontmatter-description/SKILL.md: constituent tool; not modified; orchestrated\\n- refactor-skill/SKILL.md: constituent tool; not modified; orchestrated\\n- ensure-complete/SKILL.md: constituent tool; not modified; orchestrated\\n- contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer agent: constituent tool; not modified; orchestrated\\n- plugin-lifecycle/SKILL.md: may be extended (Option B) or gain cross-reference (Option A)\\n- plugin-creator/CLAUDE.md: routing table update required in all options\\n- plugin.json / marketplace.json: auto-bumped on new skill creation (Option A only)\\n\\n## Problem\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nNo single invocation exists to take a skill or agent file and run the full set of quality improvement passes needed to bring it toward best practice. The current `contextual-ai-documentation-optimizer` agent bundles multiple concerns under one description and does not cover all quality dimensions. The missing dimensions are:\\n\\n**Language and process quality**: No agent checks for advisory language patterns (non-imperative steps, missing observable success/failure signals, unevaluable conditions, undefined actors, missing error paths). The `improve-processes` framework identifies these but is not wired into skill authoring.\\n\\n**Agent-to-skill extraction**: No agent identifies when an agent's inline content should be extracted into a skill and loaded via the frontmatter `skills:` field. Agents accumulate content that would be reusable and independently invocable as skills. No tooling surfaces this.\\n\\n**Reference drift**: No agent fetches SOURCE: URLs cited in a skill to check whether the local content still matches what the upstream source says (tracked separately as #1908, but needs to be part of a combined quality pass).\\n\\n**Where observed**: During this session, `finalize.md` was written without loading skill writing guidelines, producing advisory prose, missing observable signals, and a correctness bug (retry count mismatch). The optimizer was run afterward as remediation, not as part of the writing workflow. The correct path \u2014 load skill writing skills before writing, apply framework during writing \u2014 was not followed and had no automated enforcement.\\n\\n**Impact**:\\n- Skills and agents accumulate quality debt silently \u2014 no combined invocation to surface all gaps at once\\n- Agent-to-skill extraction opportunities are never identified; agents stay monolithic when they should load skills\\n- Language quality violations are discovered ad hoc, not as part of a standard quality pass\\n- The right path (load writing guidelines before writing) has no automated trigger\\n\\n**User-provided context** (design direction \u2014 not requirements):\\nA `/simplify`-style orchestrating skill that runs multiple focused agents in parallel, each scoped to one quality dimension (language, process edges, agent extraction, frontmatter schema, reference drift). Each agent loads the same underlying skills but follows a different path through the resources. The skill can be invoked for all passes or a named subset. Depends on the agent split in #1899 (skill-auditor, ai-doc-optimizer, skill-content-updater become the foundation agents).\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"8288fd085c721b9d223e6831c5ce2a23a772914586de48aa17396ac709ab4dd1\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg4BEQ\"}"}